 Raspberry Vanilla AOSP 15 device configuration for Raspberry Pi 5.
+
+## Serial Console Configuration
+
+### Hardware Setup
+
+Connect USB-to-serial adapter to 40-pin header:
+
+| Pin | Function | Connection |
+|-----|----------|------------|
+| 6   | GND      | GND        |
+| 8   | TXD      | USB RX     |
+| 10  | RXD      | USB TX     |
+
+### Configuration Files
+
+1. **config.txt** (`device/brcm/rpi5/boot/config.txt`)
+
+```txt
+enable_uart=1
+dtoverlay=uart0-pi5
+```
+
+2. **BoardConfig.mk** (`device/brcm/rpi5/BoardConfig.mk`)
+
+```make
+BOARD_KERNEL_CMDLINE := console=ttyAMA0,115200 no_console_suspend root=/dev/ram0 rootwait androidboot.hardware=rpi5
+```
+
+### Serial Parameters
+
+- Baud rate: 115200
+- Data bits: 8
+- Stop bits: 1
+- Parity: None
+
+### Verification
+
+After flashing the image, you should see kernel boot messages on the serial console immediately after power-on.
+
+### Troubleshooting
+
+If no serial output:
+
+1. Check USB-to-serial wiring (RX/TX swap is common)
+2. Verify serial terminal settings (115200 8N1)
+3. Ensure `config.txt` and `BoardConfig.mk` changes are compiled into boot.img
+4. Rebuild bootimage and reflash
+
+### Related UART Devices
+
+- `ttyAMA0` - 40-pin header UART (RP1 UART0, GPIO14/15)
+- `ttyAMA10` - System debug UART (not exposed on 40-pin header)
+
